<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Give a vector with magnitude <m>{10}</m> that is neither horizontal nor vertical (both components non-zero). (There are many correct answers.)</p><div><fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>You need <m>x^2 + y^2 = {10}^2 = {100}</m> with <m>x</m> and <m>y</m> both non-zero: look for two square numbers that add up to <m>{100}</m>.</p><p><m>{36} + {64} = {100}</m>, so <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} -6 \\ -8 \end{array}\right)}</m> works, and so do <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} 6 \\ 8 \end{array}\right)}</m>, <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} 8 \\ 6 \end{array}\right)}</m> and any of these with signs changed.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} -6 \\ -8 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>